      "writtenOn": "2025-04-10T20:04:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you can get away with only one set here. If you do the \"seen\" check inside `push_id` instead, you can make sure that every block is enqueued once, which means they will also only be emitted once.\n\nIt slightly changes the block emission order in certain cases (namely switch statements that re-use blocks), but I think it still works (briefly tested locally).\n\nThen you don\u0027t need the `is_stop` thing, I think.",
